---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Safe Cargo Attachment">
  <style>
    article { max-width: 72ch; }
    .meta { color: #888; font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
    .tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.7rem; padding: 1px 7px; border: 1px solid #ccc; border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 4px; }
    h2 { margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
    ul, ol { padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; line-height: 1.55; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .safety-note { background: #fff3e0; border-left: 3px solid #f0a000; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
    a.back { font-size: 0.8rem; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  </style>
  <article>
    <a href="/guides" class="back">← All guides</a>
    <h1>Safe Cargo Attachment</h1>
    <p class="meta"><span class="tag">cargo</span><span class="tag">safety</span><span class="tag">beginner</span></p>

    <p>Properly secured cargo improves handling and is essential for safe riding. The Bullitt can carry up to 100 kg — but distribution and attachment method matter.</p>

    <h2>Weight distribution</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Keep the heaviest items as low and as close to the centre of the cargo platform as possible.</li>
      <li>Avoid loading more weight on one side — uneven loads affect steering at low speed.</li>
      <li>For tall loads, keep the centre of gravity below the cargo rail height where possible.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Securing with straps</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Use cam-buckle or ratchet straps rated to at least 2× your load weight.</li>
      <li>Thread straps through the cargo rail cutouts or around rail-mounted rings.</li>
      <li>Cross straps in an X pattern over bulky items to prevent forward shifting under braking.</li>
      <li>Tuck strap tails away from wheels and pedals.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Cargo boxes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Plywood boxes: bolt through the deck with M6 bolts and large washers. Check bolt torque before each ride.</li>
      <li>Plastic bins: use rubber-backed straps to prevent sliding. Add anti-slip mat under the bin.</li>
      <li>Child seats: use only Bullitt-compatible mounting systems (e.g. Yepp, Maxi Micro, Thule Yepp Nexxt). Check that the mounting rail bolts are torqued to spec (8–10 Nm) before every ride.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="safety-note">
      <strong>Before every ride:</strong> Give loaded cargo a firm push/pull in all directions. Nothing should shift. Check that all straps and bolts are tight. For child passengers, additionally verify harness fit and seat mounting per the seat manufacturer's instructions.
    </div>

    <h2>Legal note</h2>
    <p>Regulations on carrying passengers (especially children) vary by country. Check local cycling laws. In most EU countries, child seats on cargo bikes require a certified mounting system and children must wear helmets.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
